I think the error is saying that you’ve missed a step.

!! (Bang bang) is expecting a symbol so you need to make your input variables symbols with  rlang::sym().

err_plot = function(lstat, medv) {
> lstat <-  sym(lstat)
> medv <- sym(medv)
>
> qplot(!!lstat, !!medv)
}

My favorite tutorial for tidy evaluation is here:
https://edwinth.github.io/blog/dplyr-recipes/

I know that Hadley has also updated his Advanced R book.
https://adv-r.hadley.nz/quasiquotation.html

HTH,
B

